 "seesTitle": "What the Presos cliff sees",
 "seesHTML": "From the cliff edge the ground drops straight to the shore, and the sun's entire descent path \u2014 azimuth 285\u00b0 through 290\u00b0 \u2014 is open water. Standing 80 m up dips the sea horizon 0.27\u00b0 below level, so the eclipsed sun stays visible to ~20:48, finally touching the water just left of the Portals Vells silhouette. Everything named on the far horizon sits at 290\u00b0 or further right, after the show. Stand where you can see open water in front of you, not set back from the edge.",
 "capHTML": "Horizon panorama from the Presos cliff: terrain silhouettes with projected angular altitudes against the sun's descent. The crescent is last visible at \u224820:48.",
 "recoTitle": "Around the Presos cliff",
 "recoHTML": "<li><b>The clifftop itself</b> \u2014 park on the Carretera dels Presos, walk ~200 m of open garrigue to the edge; pick footing and the way back while it's light (unfenced 80 m drop). Zero shade: water, hat, glasses, headlamp.</li><li><b>Cap Blanc lighthouse</b> (1.4 km SE) \u2014 same geometry with a parking area; busier.</li><li><b>Platja des Trenc</b> \u2014 sand instead of cliff; totality fine, crescent gone by \u224820:45.</li>",
 "verdictText": "Full show \u2014 totality, then the crescent sets into the sea at \u224820:48"
